109:For each patient, we obtained personalized gray matter atrophy pattern for each patient with depression using normative model by evaluating its deviates from the normal distribution. Following the previous studies (Bethlehem, Seidlitz, RomeroGarcia, &amp; Trakoshis, 2020; Shan et al., 2022), we trained a Gaussian process regression model to predict regional GMV from age and sex in HCs and then applied the trained model to infer regional GMV of patients. For each brain region, the Z-score was obtained by quantifying the deviation between the true GMV and the predicted one then normalized by the uncertainty of prediction (see the equation below).
113:where σ was the square root of variance (estimated from the Gaussian process regression). The positive Z-scores indicated gray matter atrophy in patients with depression compared with HCs and vice versa (Fig. 1b and 1c).
